Ethyra Intelligence — Canvas Export
===================================

This is a fork of **canvas-course-downloader** by jasp-nerd, used under the MIT
License. `LICENSE` is upstream's, retained verbatim as that licence requires,
and its terms continue to apply to everything in this repository that came from
it — which is most of the files at the top level.

    https://github.com/jasp-nerd/canvas-course-downloader

A real fork, not a rewrite
--------------------------

Upstream is a live remote (`git remote -v`), and `git fetch upstream && git merge
upstream/main` is expected to keep working. That is why the changes below are
edits in place and additions beside upstream's code, rather than a
reorganisation: when Canvas changes an endpoint, upstream usually notices first,
and a merge is how that fix arrives here.

Everything new lives under `ethyra/`. Nothing upstream has ever heard of that
directory, so it cannot collide.

What changed, and where
-----------------------

    downloader.js     modified in place, ~160 lines added behind `if (ethyra)`.
                      With `ethyra` null — every upstream code path — behaviour
                      is unchanged. See the comment on `downloadCourse`.

    manifest.json     rewritten: our name, our entry points, and three fewer
                      permissions.

    ethyra/*          original to this fork.

Still present, deliberately not loaded
--------------------------------------

`ui.js`, `content.js`, `popup.html`, `popup.js`, `background.js`, `options.*`
and `turndown*` remain in the tree and are absent from `manifest.json`.

They are kept rather than deleted so upstream merges continue to apply cleanly
to them; a merge that touches a file nothing loads is harmless. `background.js`
in particular could not be loaded even if we wanted it — it registers a
`chrome.downloads.onChanged` listener, which would force this extension to
request a `downloads` permission it never uses and could not justify at review.

What this fork does NOT inherit
-------------------------------

Upstream mirrors an entire Canvas course to disk — course files, pages, modules,
discussions, announcements, quizzes — for teachers and students alike, and
writes it as human-readable HTML or Markdown.

This one collects **one student's own coursework only**, emits it as
machine-readable JSON alongside the files, and uploads it to Ethyra. The scope is
narrowed by configuration (`ethyra/profile.js`) rather than by deletion, so the
code upstream maintains is still here and still mergeable.

Third-party dependencies
------------------------

    client-zip   MIT, Touffy — https://github.com/Touffy/client-zip
                 Vendored by upstream as a minified build, unmodified.

Branding
--------

`icons/` is still upstream's artwork and the extension name is ours. That
mismatch is fine for local development and must be resolved before any Chrome
Web Store submission.

Student data
------------

This extension reads a student's own Canvas coursework — assignment
instructions, submissions, grades and instructor comments — and transmits it to
Ethyra for analysis. That is education data subject to FERPA, and it is a
material difference from upstream, which sends nothing anywhere. See PRIVACY.md.
